<article class="env-exercise" id="078L">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/078L">Exercise <span data-tag="078L">111.2.4</span>.</a> Let $(I, \geq )$ be a directed set and let $(A_ i, \varphi _{ij})$ be a system of rings over $I$ with colimit $A$. Prove that there is a bijection </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A) = \{ (\mathfrak p_ i)_{i \in I} \mid \mathfrak p_ i \subset A_ i \text{ and } \mathfrak p_ i = \varphi _{ij}^{-1}(\mathfrak p_ j)\  \forall i \leq j\}  \subset \prod \nolimits _{i \in I} \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A_ i)  \]
</div>
  <p> The set on the right hand side of the equality is the limit of the sets $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A_ i)$. Notation $\mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A_ i)$. </p>
</article>